---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="FAQ — Surfboard Repairs Mount Maunganui | Solar Surf">
  <section class="faq-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>SURFBOARD REPAIR FAQ</h1>
      <p class="faq-sub">Straight answers from the Mount's original surf shop. Since 1974.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container faq-body">
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h2 id="how-long">How long does a surfboard ding repair take?</h2>
      <p>Repairs usually take <strong>just a few days</strong>. Small dings can be quicker; snapped boards and major damage take longer depending on the extent. Re-finishing work (clean, speed finish, de-waxing) is usually a few days too. Call us on <a href="tel:0275888082">027 5888 082</a> and we'll give you a realistic timeframe for your board.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h2 id="cost">How much does surfboard repair cost in New Zealand?</h2>
      <p>Typical pricing at our Mount Maunganui workshop:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Ding repairs: <strong>from $60</strong></li>
        <li>Medium damage / rail repairs: <strong>from $80</strong></li>
        <li>Snapped board repair: <strong>quoted after inspection</strong></li>
        <li>Re-finishing — strip and clean all the old wax and grime, then re-finish with spray finish and wet and dry sanding for maximum performance: <strong>from $100</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>We always quote before we start</strong> — no surprises, ever. Send us a photo of the damage via our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or text it to 027 5888 082 and we'll quote before you commit to anything.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h2 id="boards">What kinds of boards do you repair?</h2>
      <p>Shortboards, longboards, fish, guns, mid-lengths, softboards, SUPs (stand-up paddleboards), windsurf boards, and foil boards. If it's fibreglass, epoxy, or composite construction and it goes in the water, we can almost certainly fix it. We've been repairing every board type the Mount's surfers ride since 1974.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h2 id="booking">Do I need to book, or can I just drop my board off?</h2>
      <p>Drop-offs are welcome any day of the week — someone is usually at the workshop between <strong>9:30am and 4:00pm</strong>, 7 days, at Unit 8, 21 MacDonald Street, Mount Maunganui. If nobody's in Unit 8, <strong>Mike in Unit 9 next door can take your board for drop-off or pickup</strong>. A quick text with a photo of the damage means we can have materials ready and quote you before you arrive.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h2 id="where">Where are you located?</h2>
      <p>Unit 8, 21 MacDonald Street, Mount Maunganui 3116 — just minutes from the Mount's main breaks. We're the Mount's original surf shop, operating since 1974.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h2 id="worth-it">Is my board worth repairing, or should I just buy a new one?</h2>
      <p>Honest answer: most dings cost far less to repair professionally than the damage costs you in the water. An unrepaired ding absorbs water, rots the foam core, and turns a $90 fix into a dead board. If the structural damage is beyond economic repair, we'll tell you straight — we've been doing this for 50 years, and a straight answer keeps surfers coming back.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h2 id="turnaround">Do you do same-day repairs?</h2>
      <p>Sometimes — small dings can occasionally be turned around same-day, but realistically most repairs take a few days depending on the queue and resin curing times. Text ahead with a photo and we'll tell you honestly what timeframe to expect for your board.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h2 id="history">How long have you been repairing surfboards?</h2>
      <p>Solar Surf has operated in Mount Maunganui since 1974 — we're the Mount's original surf shop. Fifty years of repairs, restorations, and shaper experience. Read the full story on our <a href="/#story">Our Story</a> section.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-cta">
      <h3>Damaged your board?</h3>
      <p>Text a photo to <a href="tel:0275888082">027 5888 082</a> for a fast quote, or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How long does a surfboard ding repair take?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Repairs usually take just a few days. Small dings can be quicker; snapped boards and major damage take longer depending on the extent. Re-finishing (clean, speed finish, de-waxing) is usually a few days too." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How much does surfboard repair cost in New Zealand?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "At Solar Surf Mount Maunganui: ding repairs from $60, medium damage and rail repairs from $80, snapped boards quoted after inspection, and re-finishing from $100. Re-finishing means stripping and cleaning all the old wax and grime from the board, then re-finishing with spray finish and wet and dry sanding for maximum performance. We always quote before we start - no surprises. Send a photo for an exact quote." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What kinds of boards do you repair?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Shortboards, longboards, fish, mid-lengths, softboards, SUPs, windsurf boards and foil boards - any fibreglass, epoxy or composite watercraft." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do I need to book, or can I drop my board off?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Drop-offs are welcome 7 days a week - someone is usually at the workshop between 9:30am and 4:00pm at Unit 8, 21 MacDonald Street, Mount Maunganui. If nobody's in, Mike in Unit 9 next door can take your board for drop-off or pickup. No appointment needed." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Where is Solar Surf located?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Unit 8, 21 MacDonald Street, Mount Maunganui 3116, New Zealand. Phone 027 5888 082." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is my board worth repairing or should I buy a new one?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Most dings cost far less to repair professionally than the water damage they cause if left unrepaired. If the damage is beyond economic repair, Solar Surf will say so honestly." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Do you do same-day surfboard repairs?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Small dings can occasionally be turned around same-day, but most repairs take a few days depending on the queue and resin curing times. Text ahead with a photo for an honest timeframe." }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How long have you been repairing surfboards?",
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Solar Surf has operated in Mount Maunganui since 1974 - the Mount's original surf shop, with 50 years of repair and restoration experience." }
      }
    ]
  })} />
</Layout>

<style>
  .faq-hero { padding: 90px 0 40px; text-align: center; }
  .faq-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.5rem); }
  .faq-sub { color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 12px; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .faq-body { max-width: 800px; padding-bottom: 60px; }
  .faq-item { padding: 28px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.12); }
  .faq-item h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--text); }
  .faq-item p, .faq-item li { color: var(--text-dim); line-height: 1.7; }
  .faq-item ul { margin: 12px 0 12px 20px; }
  .faq-item strong { color: var(--sun); }
  .faq-item a { color: var(--cyan); }
  .faq-cta { margin-top: 48px; padding: 32px; background: var(--deep); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 107, 26, 0.3); border-radius: 8px; text-align: center; }
  .faq-cta h3 { color: var(--sun); font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .faq-cta a { color: var(--cyan); font-weight: 600; }
</style>